   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Ordering",
     "texto": [
      "To order something: thing + **を ください** (please give me…) or, more politely, **を おねがいします** (…please). **メニュー を ください** (please give me the menu).",
      "When you walk into any shop or restaurant you'll be greeted with **いらっしゃいませ** (welcome). You don't need to reply.",
      "To call the waiter: **すみません**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Prices",
     "texto": [
      "The currency is the yen: **えん**. Prices are big numbers, so you need the hundreds and the thousands.",
      "**ひゃく** is 100 and **せん** is 1,000. They are multiplied by putting the number in front: **にひゃく** (200), **ごせん** (5,000).",
      "Some change their sound: 300 is **さんびゃく**, 600 is **ろっぴゃく**, 800 is **はっぴゃく**; 3,000 is **さんぜん** and 8,000 is **はっせん**.",
      "Japanese counts in units of ten thousand: 10,000 is **いちまん**."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
